  "description": "PORTSMOUTH, Va. — The Coast Guard medevacs a 52-year-old woman from a cruise ship approximately 51 miles east of Elizabeth City, N.C., Oct. 23, 2012. Personnel aboard the Carnival Glory, a 952-foot cruise ship, contacted Coast Guard 5th District watchstanders at approximately 10:30 p.m. Oct. 22, reporting a woman aboard was experiencing chest pains and requesting a medevac. U.S. Coast Guard video released by D5 Public Affairs. There is no audio on this clip.",
